Z||000000||william_thorniii||03-28-2000||01:33 AM||||Friends,<P>As many of you know, I am in the process of replacing my gauges with some from Super X.  As I am nearing installation... I just can't finish untill I can find something to do with these needles.  They appear to be a clear material lined on the back with an orange paint.  Aside from the suggestions that have already been given me about the reflective paint and the like in my other thread... are there any suggestions?  <P>Many Thanks,<P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||5
Z||000001||TOM||03-28-2000||04:57 PM||||I am in the process of taking out those faces and going back to the stock ones.||||reg||1
Z||000002||WisconsinGT||03-28-2000||06:39 PM||||William, the magic solution for the needle color is Testers Floresent orange. This is waht I was told by the man. (Ed Parks)||||reg||1
